1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Step thirteen. The agent deletes your
tests.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Step fourteen. It overwrites the config.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Git status agrees. Two test files, gone.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,500
There were three. The third was never
committed. Git can't return it.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,500
But rewindagents recorded all fourteen
steps.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Step twelve was the last good one.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,500
So rewind to it.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Four files back: all three tests and the
config.

9
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,000
And the rewind is step fifteen. You can
undo the undo.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The first twelve steps stay. So does the
new test.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Every tool call goes into a hash-chained
log. Edit one record and verify names it.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,500
Before every edit, the hook copies the
file as it is.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,100
Around every Bash command it saves first,
scans after.

14
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,500
So step thirteen kept three copies.

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:57,000
rewindagents install adds the Claude Code
hook. It has run in real sessions.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,800
Codex and Cursor: built from the vendors'
hook documentation, tested with the

17
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,000
documented payloads. Not yet in a live
session.

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,438
Files over twenty megabytes aren't copied.

19
00:01:07,438 --> 00:01:11,500
Over twenty thousand files, no scan, and
rewind says so.

20
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,000
Export it as one HTML page. Find it later
with sessions.

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Apache-2.0, standard library only. Not on
PyPI yet: install from the repository.

22
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
A paid Cloud tier is planned. Not built,
not priced.

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,500
Your editor has had undo for decades. Now
your agent does.
